  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- **`IAsyncLockCE` let work started while it was held enter it later, while another flow held it.** Such work, a task say, inherits the holder's flow, and the lock counted a flow's entrances in it, so the work found itself counted in and entered without waiting, even after the hold had ended. A lock meant to keep two flows apart let them in at once. The work may still enter while the hold lasts, and the lock stays held until it leaves too; once the hold has ended, it takes its turn as any other flow does.\n- **Requires newer minor versions of other Compze packages:** Compze.Threading 0.14.0-alpha (was 0.13.0-alpha). Upgrading to this version upgrades each package listed here too, so their changelogs apply to this upgrade as well.",
